==English==
===Noun===
'''dyspepsia''' 

# {{pathology}} Dyspepsia ia a cluster of symptoms which usually arise from disorders or dysfunction of the stomach. It can include pain or discomfort in the upper abdomen, bloating, belching or nausea often following a meal. Dyspepsia is sometimes accompanied by heartburn, a burning sensation in the midline of the chest.
Dyspepsia is usually caused by lifestyle factors such as overeating or excess alcohol but is sometimes caused by serious pathology such as peptic ulcers or cancers of the stomach.
